# SAEA-BENCH-buf90w/buf120/buf180 — the window frontier the freed HBM pays
# for (owner directive 2026-08-12: mmproj-to-CPU's larger value = longer
# slices; verify the optimum). Wide shape -c 65536 -np 16 (4,096/slot)
# fits at ~21.2 GB without mmproj. buf90w REruns the 90 s point on the wide
# shape as the cross-shape bridge (90 s narrow = 13.35); buf120/180 extend
# the curve (sized: 120 s ~1,772 audio tok, 180 s ~2,545; decode ~230-350 s
# vs the 420 s timeout - tight at 180, watched). New cuts are cold encodes.
# run_id:baseline_fragment
SAEA-BENCH-buf90w:fixed-batch-bare16-buf90
SAEA-BENCH-buf120:fixed-batch-bare16-buf120
SAEA-BENCH-buf180:fixed-batch-bare16-buf180
